  "request_id": "efficient-language-patterns-20260929",
  "title": "各語言高效撰寫模式與編譯器優化參數入法",
  "summary": "Human-governor directive 2026-09-29: codify the per-language efficient-writing patterns (C++ move/string_view/reserve; C# ValueTask/Span/struct; F# tail recursion/seq/Struct-DU; Go value-over-pointer/make-capacity/strings.Builder/sync.Pool/no blind goroutines; Rust slice-str-no-clone/iterators/with_capacity) and the compiler optimization rule (production uses the owner release profile: /O2 or -O3+LTO, cargo release, Release+optimize+TieredPGO, optimized Go release + trimpath, Julia -O3; unoptimized/debug never ships and the profile is recorded in B79 toolchain/ABI evidence). B157 carries the clause, metadata registers the patterns, the architecture artifact carries the same generation. Codex-only change: no implementation is modified by this request.",
  "requested_by": "decision-sovereign",
  "origin": "human-governor directive: C++/C#/F#/Go/Rust 高效寫法；善用編譯器優化參數",
  "change_class": "authority-duty",
